      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "The definition of flying object is very weirdly specific and not particularly useful.\n2. c) ii) is also very strange\n\nDoesnt say much about Airspace safety enforcement at all which I find weird, would I allowed to kinetically intercept any aircraft that clipped the airspace? do I need to provide warning over comms?\nDo I need to provide com-system independent warning? \nWhats with aircraft identification? \nCan I shoot at a plane that shuts off its transponder assuming its now a valid target under 4.b?\n\nI very much vote **AGAINST** and encourage you to do the same",
